# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.
#
# Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is shipped to the browser in plain text.
# If it must stay secret, it must not carry that prefix — and it must only be
# read in server code.

# Required in production so confirmation emails link here, not localhost.
# Vercel Production: https://sprachenlernen.vercel.app
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Supabase (ADR-0007). URL and publishable key are safe to expose — access is
# enforced by row-level security, not by keeping these secret. The elevated key
# bypasses RLS entirely and must NEVER carry the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix or be used
# outside server-only code — in practice, `lib/db/` only.
#
# Publishable/secret replaced anon/service_role as the key pair Supabase issues;
# the legacy JWT pair still works and is deprecated at the end of 2026. The
# elevated variable below keeps the legacy name because that is the key the
# project is configured with — rename it in the same change that rotates to an
# sb_secret_ key, never before, or the running deployment loses its credential.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Migrations only, never read by the app. The access token authenticates the
# Supabase CLI against the Management API; the database password is what
# `supabase db push` connects with. Neither belongs in a browser bundle.
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=
